Third-party materials
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Model weights are NOT redistributed by this repository. They are downloaded from
the Hugging Face Hub at build time (`make demo` / `uv run quettos download`) into
the gitignored build/ directory. The models used are:

  * Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct
    Copyright Alibaba Cloud. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct

  * SmolLM2-135M-Instruct
    Copyright Hugging Face. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-135M-Instruct

Evaluation data (not redistributed; downloaded on demand into the gitignored
build/ directory, used only for quality measurement and never shipped in any
artifact):

  * WikiText-2 (Merity, Xiong, Bradbury, Socher, 2016)
    Text extracted from English Wikipedia, under Creative Commons
    Attribution-ShareAlike terms: the dataset card records CC BY-SA 3.0 and the
    GFDL in its metadata and CC BY-SA 4.0 in its licensing section.
    Archive fetched by `uv run quettos corpus` (sw/quettos/corpus.py):
    https://wikitext.smerity.com/wikitext-2-raw-v1.zip
    Dataset card: https://huggingface.co/datasets/Salesforce/wikitext

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived artifacts
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following files, where present in this repository or published as release
assets, are derived works of the model weights listed above and are made
available under the Apache License, Version 2.0, the same license that governs
the source weights:

  * models/<model>/calib.json          (calibration maxima and per-class formats)
  * models/<model>/expected_tokens.json (greedy tokens produced by the integer golden model)
  * models/<model>/quality.json        (the measured quality of the integer model
                                        against the float32 reference)
  * the tool-call prefix KV-cache release asset (`make regen-prefix`)

Per-model layout.json, program.lst and sha256 files describe the compiled image
and are derived from the same weights.

The held-out rows of quality.json are measurements over WikiText-2 as well as
over the weights. That file carries per-window statistics -- top-1 agreement,
KL, NLL and perplexity -- beside the SHA-256 of the archive, of the member read
out of it and of the token ids scored, and it carries no text and no token ids
from the corpus; the archive itself stays in the gitignored build/corpus/ and
is redistributed neither here nor as a release asset. WikiText-2 is credited
above, as its Attribution-ShareAlike terms ask.
